    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Hanafuda (花札)',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Hanafuda (花札, 'flower cards') are traditional Japanese playing cards comprising a 48-card deck divided into 12 suits, each representing a month and featuring a specific flower or plant. Hanafuda is not a single game but a family of games, most commonly fishing/capture games where players match cards from their hand with cards on the field. Popular games include Koi-Koi, Hachi-Hachi, and Hana-Awase. Cards are categorized as Brights, Animals, Ribbons, and Plains, with varying point values.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Hanafuda cards originated in 18th-century Japan, evolving from Portuguese playing cards. The Japanese government banned Western-style cards, leading to the development of Hanafuda as a workaround.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2 to 6 players depending on the specific Hanafuda game (e.g. Koi-Koi typically 2).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '48 cards divided into 12 suits (months):\n- January (Pine), February (Plum), March (Cherry), April (Wisteria), May (Iris), June (Peony), July (Bush Clover), August (Pampas Grass), September (Chrysanthemum), October (Maple), November (Willow), December (Paulownia).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Each suit has 4 cards, categorized as:\n- **Brights** (20 points): Special high-value cards.\n- **Animals** (10 points): Cards featuring animals.\n- **Ribbons** (5 points): Cards with ribbons or poetry.\n- **Plains/Chaff** (1 point): Simple flower cards.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Hanafuda deck (48 cards).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Varies by game; typically dealer distributes cards to hands and table.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
